---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SUPPORT_URL } from '../config/site.mjs';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Privacy — Ladle"
	description="Ladle collects nothing about you. No account, no analytics, no tracking, in the app or on this website."
	current="privacy"
>
	<div class="container page">
		<header class="intro">
			<p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
			<h1 class="disp">Ladle collects nothing about you.</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				No account, no analytics, no tracking, in the app or on this website. Here’s exactly what goes
				where, in plain words.
			</p>
			<p class="updated">Updated October 2026</p>
		</header>

		<div class="summary glass">
			<ul>
				<li><Icon name="check" size={16} strokeWidth={2.4} class="ink" />No account, analytics or telemetry</li>
				<li><Icon name="check" size={16} strokeWidth={2.4} class="ink" />Your downloads and history stay on your Mac</li>
				<li><Icon name="check" size={16} strokeWidth={2.4} class="ink" />No cookies or analytics on this website</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>The app</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Ladle sends nothing about you anywhere.</strong> There’s no account, no analytics and no
					telemetry. Ladle doesn’t know who you are and doesn’t report how you use it.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Its only network traffic is the downloads you start and one update check a day.</strong>{' '}
					Ladle connects to the sites you download from, and nowhere else, apart from that check.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>The update check sends only Ladle’s version and your macOS version.</strong> It reads the
					update feed from this website. New versions of Ladle download from GitHub Releases. You can turn the
					check off in <strong>Ladle › Settings › Updates</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Your download history stays on your Mac</strong>, in Ladle’s folder inside{' '}
					<code>~/Library/Application Support</code>. Remove a download from the list, or delete that folder,
					and it’s gone.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Your clipboard is read on your Mac and never sent.</strong> Ladle looks at it only to spot a
					link to a file you might want to download. Turn this off with{' '}
					<strong>Watch the clipboard for links</strong> in <strong>Ladle › Settings › General</strong>.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Cookies and referrers stay with their site.</strong> When a download comes from your browser,
					Ladle sends the cookies and page address that came with it only to the site the file comes from.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>The browser extension</h2>
			<p>
				Ladle’s extension looks at the downloads you click and the videos on the page you’re viewing, so it
				can hand downloads to Ladle and show the Download video button. When it hands over a download, it
				passes the file’s link, the page it came from, its name and the cookies that site needs, directly to
				Ladle on your Mac. It doesn’t keep or send a record of your browsing.
			</p>

			<h2>This website</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking scripts and no ads.</strong></li>
				<li>
					<strong>Fonts come from this site</strong>, not from a font service, so loading a page doesn’t tell
					anyone else you visited.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Two preferences stay in your browser:</strong> your light or dark theme, and which browser
					you picked in the docs. They’re kept in your browser’s local storage, on your device, and never sent
					anywhere.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages</strong>, and Ladle’s downloads come from GitHub Releases.
					Like any web host, GitHub receives the usual request details, such as your IP address, when you load a
					page or download a file. We don’t get visitor logs or statistics from it. GitHub’s{' '}
					<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>{' '}
					covers what it does with that information.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Support</h2>
			<p>
				Support happens on <a href={SUPPORT_URL}>GitHub Issues</a>, which are public. Anything you post there,
				including links and logs, can be read by anyone, so leave out private download links and personal
				details.
			</p>

			<h2>If anything changes</h2>
			<p>
				If Ladle or this website ever handles your information differently, this page will be updated first and
				the change will be called out in the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.page {
		max-width: 820px;
		padding-top: 56px;
		padding-bottom: 96px;
	}
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 14px;
	}
	h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 60px);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.02;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	.lead {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--ld-text2);
	}
	.updated {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 14px;
		color: var(--ld-text3);
	}
	.summary {
		margin: 32px 0 8px;
		padding: 22px 26px;
		border-radius: 24px;
	}
	.summary ul {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
		font-size: 16px;
		font-weight: 500;
	}
	.summary li {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.summary :global(.ink) {
		color: var(--ld-ink);
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.page {
			padding-top: 32px;
		}
	}
</style>
